        "original_id": "179e60a2-d6f0-5584-ad0a-588826a9e5bd",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Huell Howser\n- Works: California's Gold, Winnie the Pooh (2011), Malibu Public Beach Safari\n- Organizations: KCET, California PBS stations, Disney\n- Topics: LA Urban Rangers, media coverage\n\nFacts:\n- Huell Howser was born on October 18, 1945, and died on January 7, 2013.\n- Huell Howser was an American television personality, actor, producer, writer, singer, and voice artist.\n- Huell Howser was best known for hosting, producing, and writing California's Gold.\n- KCET in Los Angeles produced California's Gold for California PBS stations.\n- Winnie the Pooh, released in 2011, was the 51st Disney animated feature film.\n- Huell Howser voiced the Backson in Winnie the Pooh (2011).\n- The LA Urban Rangers' longest-running and most recent outing was the Malibu Public Beach Safari.\n- The Malibu Public Beach Safari was featured in media reports and by Huell Howser on his show.",
